===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|hasel}}, from {{inh|en|ang|hæsl|t=hazel, shrub}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*hasl}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*haslaz|t=hazel}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*kóslos|t=hazel}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|hazelaar||hazel}}, {{cog|de|Hasel||hazel}}, {{cog|sv|hassel||hazel}}, {{cog|la|corulus}}, {{m|la|corylus||hazel-tree, hazelwood}}, {{cog|ga|coll||hazel}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈheɪzəl/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-hazel.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪzəl|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[tree]] or [[shrub]] of the genus {{taxfmt|Corylus|genus}}, bearing edible nuts called [[hazelnut]]s or [[filbert]]s.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1895|author=S. R. Crockett|title=A Cry Across the Black Water|passage=The green turf was velvet underfoot. The blackbirds fluted in the '''hazels''' there.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1940|author=Rosetta E. Clarkson|title=Green Enchantments: The Magic Spell of Gardens |publisher=The Macmillan Company|page=273|text=Have a tree or two the witches particularly like, such as the alder, larch, cypress and hemlock; then, to counteract any possible evil effects, there must be a holly, yew, '''hazel''', elder, mountain ash or juniper.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} The [[nut]] of the hazel [[tree]].
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The wood of a hazelnut tree.
# {{lb|en|countable|and|uncountable}} A greenish-brown colour, the colour of a ripe hazelnut.
#: {{color panel|A67B5B}}
# {{lb|en|mining|countable}} [[freestone|Freestone]].<ref>{{R:Raymond Glossary|page=48}}</ref>

