===Adjective===
{{en-adj|more|er|comp2_qual=rare|sup2_qual=rare}}

# Of a [[greenish]]-[[brown]] [[colour]]. (often used to refer to eye colour)
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=James L. Collings|title=Syndicates: Oh Marie! Whatta Gal and Whatta Reporter|editor=Robert U[tting] Brown|journal=w:Editor & Publisher|volume=89|issue=1|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=Editor & Publisher Co., Inc.|date=7 January 1956|page=40|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/sim_editor-publisher_1956-01-07_89_1/page/40/mode/1up|column=1|issn=0013-094X|passage=As she grew up and her hazel eyes became '''hazeler''' and her dark hair darker and her white skin whiter, and her form a sigh on every boy’s lips, she concentrated on one dream.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Robyn Donald|chapter=4|title=A Willing Surrender|location=London|publisher=[[w:Mills & Boon|Mills & Boon Limited]]|year=1986|page=81|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/willingsurrender0000dona/page/81/mode/1up|isbn=0 263 75403 0|passage=The shrewd eyes, more '''hazel''' than her son’s but with the same straight brows, were fixed on Clary’s face.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Adryan Russ; Doug Haverty|chapter=Act Two|title=[[w:Inside Out (musical)|Inside Out]]|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=w:Samuel French, Inc.|year=1996|page=58|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/insideout0000have/page/58/mode/1up|isbn=0 573 60032 5|passage=SAGE: Don’t my eyes look '''hazeler'''? (<!--upright-->''or: periwinkler)'' / CHLO: ''(as GARTH)'' Yes. / SAGE: You said you loved my hazel eyes. ''(or: periwinkle)'' Don’t you love them more hazely? ''(or: periwinkly)''}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Sharon Smith|chapter=2|title=Into the Dark|location=Nederland, Tex.|publisher=Yellow Rose Books|year=2005|page=12|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/intodark00shar/page/12/mode/1up|isbn=1-932300-38-4|passage=The drummer’s eyes took the small woman in slowly, starting with her face, down to her feet and then back up into the '''hazelest''' eyes she’d ever seen.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Doug Brod|title=Burning Sensation|editor=w:Sia Michel|journal=[[w:Spin (magazine)|Spin]]|volume=21|issue=12|location=New York, N.Y.|month=December|year=2005|page=73|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=4HSJOu6uEvUC&pg=PA73|column=2|issn=0886-3032|passage=What’s that line on “[[w:One Way Ticket to Hell... and Back#Track listing|Hazel Eyes]]”: “I’ve never seen a set of eyes more '''hazeler'''”? {{quote-gloss|{{w|Justin Hawkins}}:}} “I’ve never seen a set of eyes more hazelerer.”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Margaret Fiske|chapter=Sense & Circuitry: Cyberth 1813|editors=Peter Archer; Jennifer Lawler|title=Bad Austen: The Worst Stories Jane Never Wrote|location=Avon, Mass.|publisher=Adams Media, [[w:F+W|F+W Media, Inc.]]|year=2011|section=part 2 (If Jane Could See Us Now)|page=96|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/badaustenworstst0000unse/page/96/mode/1up|isbn=978-1-4405-1185-1|passage=Doolittle had the '''hazelest''' eyeballs, the winsomest spinal pelt.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Francine J. Colangelo|chapter=10|title=Marah Hein: The Legend of a Viking Woman|location=Bloomington, Ind.|publisher=Balboa Press, {{w|Hay House}}|date=8 March 2012|page=84|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=doipxCKr_t4C&pg=PA84|isbn=978-1-4525-4719-0|passage=His eyes were somewhere indefinite between green and hazel. Sometimes appearing '''hazeler''' or greener depending on how the light flickered on them.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Becky Albertalli|chapter=16|title=w:The Upside of Unrequited|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=Balzer + Bray, [[w:HarperCollins|HarperCollins Publishers]]|date=11 April 2017|page=178|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/upsideofunrequit0000albe/page/178/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-06-234870-8|passage=And now I should probably say something, but that would involve words, and WHAT EVEN ARE WORDS, and he’s looking at me with the '''hazelest''' eyes and the softest, most upturned mouth.}}

